            <div xml:id="d137">

                <pb facs="0246" n="170" xml:id="pg170"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">660F.116/159: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Czechoslovakia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wright</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Praha</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-03-04T11:00:00+01:00">March 4, 1935—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 4—9:56 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>11. My telegram No. 9, February 19, 4 p.m. Foreign Office now informs me that
                    Czech-German Clearing Committee has determined to recommend to respective
                    Governments that part payments in marks for cotton be at rate 2½ percent and for
                    other shipments upon percentage basis equivalent to expenses attendant all
                    transactions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wright</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
